Z||000000||terryk||10-24-1999||09:49 PM||||I need to replace the muffler, et al on my 86 SE V6. There is no leak, but it sounds like the guts came loose and are resonating. Horrible.<P>How is the Fiero Store on delivery? Any other recommendations for a source for the stock system. Cat back. Hell at this point I might as will take it from before the cat back.<P>I don't want to install a non-factory setup.<P>Thanks for any suggestions.<P>Terry<p>[This message has been edited by terryk (edited 10-25-1999).]||||reg||1
Z||000001||88 Fiero||10-24-1999||10:15 PM||||terryk...guys on my club Fieros West uses the Flowmasters for the Camaro RS...they sound good and mean....||||reg||1
Z||000002||lowCG||10-25-1999||12:01 AM||||I'm thinking that'll be a project for me in the near future also.<BR>Flowmaster mufflers sound great on everything I've heard them on,how much do the muffler shops charge to install/create a new,larger system to go with it? <BR>Terry,you might be able and reduce the rattling temporarily by denting the muffler in the right spot with a hammer,or squeezing it with a large clamp,and something under it.<p>[This message has been edited by lowCG (edited 10-25-1999).]||||reg||1
Z||000003||BENGAL4||10-25-1999||10:36 AM||||Terryk,<P>Do not, I repeat do not purchase an exhaust system from the Fiero Store. I purchased a Ocelot system and I am not happy at all with it. It sounds terrible and when I got it, the exhaust tips did not fit so I had to go to a muffler shop to get the pipes expanded. Also, the bracket to attach the springs to the muffler are missing. I called them and they said they don't put the bracket on the muffler because they said you don't need them. I am rebuilding a 2.8 and I am going to get a Flowmaster and do a custom system using the stock tips. As for the Ocelot, I will take a loss and wish I had researched it more. ||||reg||8
Z||000004||87GT||10-25-1999||12:08 PM||||I bought the Ocelot system from the fiero store also.  It sounds okay, but the chrome tips that came with it already have rust building on them.  I always clean them but the rust is there.  ||||reg||1
Z||000005||WisconsinGT||10-25-1999||01:06 PM||||Why is everyone talking Flowmaster? I was under the impression that "Borla" is the king of the hill when it comes to exhaust. Please educate me. Thanks||||reg||1
Z||000006||terryk||10-25-1999||07:22 PM||||Thanks for the comments! I wasn't thinking of getting the Ocelot system (too much for too little). Anyone bought the standard $179 77355 system?<P>Ok so other than being crap, the delivery time as ok?<P>I could get the Fiero Heaven system for $1k, but I figured that would be too gaudy. ||||reg||12
Z||000007||batboy||10-25-1999||09:38 PM||||Wisconsin, the FlowMaster mufflers are very efficient high performance mufflers that have a lower tone and are slightly louder than stock, but quieter and better sounding than glasspacks.||||reg||1
Z||000008||Bruce||10-25-1999||09:46 PM||||I purchased a flowmaster that I plan to install with a new cat. converter and larger tubing. Are there major modifications necessary to accomodate the flowmaster.<BR>(Soon, DXR_DAD, soon.........)||||reg||5
Z||000009||superXmotorsports||10-25-1999||10:02 PM||||I installed the Borla XR1 system a couple months ago on my 3.2L 87 GT.  The sound is very mellow (I like it loud) but the performance was as good as the straight pipes I had on it before.  The tips look a little wimpy (like the Ocelot system) but I installed larger Cone duals tips and it looks alot better.  You can see pictures of both on my website (under construction) <A HREF="http://users.desupernet.net/superx" TARGET=_blank>http://users.desupernet.net/superx</A> <P>By the way I just purchased another 87 GT and it has the Ocelot system and I didn't care for the resonation at about 4000 RPM.<BR>||||reg||6
Z||000010||terryk||10-25-1999||10:48 PM||||2 chamber Flowmasters cause small animals to die as you drive by. No thanks. I installed one my Ciera and promptly took it off.<P>Ok, I've lost it. I'm replying to my own posts.......<p>[This message has been edited by terryk (edited 10-25-1999).]||||reg||1
Z||000011||lowCG||10-26-1999||01:55 AM||||The sizing would be very critical with a Flowmaster;there's no packing,it's all depending on the cancellation pressure waves or whatever.I've heard them on pumped up V8s that sound great,but I'll bet they're  touchy as to the pulses of the engine,tubing size on the rest of the system,and the placement of the vanes inside.<BR>Probably easier to get an all around good sound/flow with large resonators of some kind,unless the Flowmaster for the Fiero(Camaro RS) sounds really good or something.<BR>BTW,which motor,or does it matter for the Camaro flowmaster muffler application?||||reg||1
